# Conformance probe pack for value transforms (spec 0.15) in a sequential
# `bits` layout, most-significant-bit-first (ruling 3). Public. No kinds.
# Exercises transforms at bit positions that are not byte boundaries; an
# absent `chars` key, which writes zero bits and not padding (ruling 16), so
# an absent icao6 callsign writes codes 0, which do not decode; and the empty
# text, present, in an `opt` block (ruling 13), which sets the bit.
#
#   time_ms 40 (uiscale:1/1000, microseconds) | c1 6 (smag) |
#   callsign 18 (3 icao6 characters) | opt bit | opt: s1 12 (2 ais6
#   characters) | s2 9 (3 octal digits) | zero bits to the byte
format     conformance-transforms-seq
version    0.15.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       probe
wire       bits
layout     sequential
bit_order  msb
field   time_ms   40  uiscale:1/1000
field   probe.c1  6   smag
field   callsign  18  chars:icao6
opt
  field  probe.s1  12  chars:ais6
end
field   probe.s2  9   octal
